                "title": "Mexico Hotel",
                "url": "https://horwathhtl.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Mexico-Hotel-Market-2024.pdf?utm_source=openai"
              },
              {
                "type": "url_citation",
                "end_index": 2375,
                "start_index": 2284,
                "title": "Autograph Collection Hotels | Premium Marriott Hotels",
                "url": "https://autograph-hotels.marriott.com/?utm_source=openai"
              }
            ],
            "logprobs": [],
            "text": "For an **upper-upscale hotel project in Mexico**, owners typically begin with the major global systems—Marriott, Hilton, Hyatt, IHG and Accor—plus Grupo Posadas because of its strong domestic distribution. These groups also account for much of Mexico’s active hotel-development pipeline. ([horwathhtl.com](https://horwathhtl.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Mexico-Hotel-Market-2024.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Common first-round shortlist\n\n| Hotel group | Brands commonly considered | Typical positioning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | **Westin, Sheraton, Renaissance, Marriott Hotels, Le Méridien** | Traditional or lifestyle-oriented full-service upper-upscale |\n|  | **Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio** | Soft brands for distinctive, locally designed or conversion properties |\n| **Hilton** | **Hilton Hotels & Resorts, DoubleTree by Hilton** | Full-service corporate, meetings and leisure |\n|  | **Curio Collection, Canopy by Hilton** | Independent/lifestyle or neighborhood-driven projects |\n| **Hyatt** | **Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric** | Regency for larger full-service/convention hotels; Centric for lifestyle urban locations |\n|  | **JdV by Hyatt, The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** | Boutique or independent concepts; Unbound can extend into luxury |\n| **IHG** | **Crowne Plaza, Hotel Indigo, voco** | Corporate full service, boutique lifestyle and conversion-friendly positioning |\n| **Accor** | **Pullman, Swissôtel, Mövenpick** | International premium/upper-upscale |\n|  | **MGallery** | Collection brand for distinctive boutique or heritage properties |\n| **Grupo Posadas** | **Grand Fiesta Americana, Fiesta Americana, Curamoria Collection** | Strong Mexican recognition and domestic commercial platform |\n|  | **Live Aqua** | Usually considered when the project can support a luxury or upper-upscale-plus positioning |\n\nMarriott officially places Westin, Sheraton, Renaissance, Le Méridien, Marriott Hotels and its collection brands within its premium full-service portfolio. Hyatt identifies Hyatt Regency and Hyatt Centric as upper-upscale and The Unbound Collection as upper-upscale/luxury. IHG groups Crowne Plaza, voco and related brands in its premium portfolio, while Accor identifies Pullman, Swissôtel and Mövenpick as premium brands. ([autograph-hotels.marriott.com](https://autograph-hotels.marriott.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\n### If it is a resort or all-inclusive project\n\nThe shortlist usually expands to include:\n\n- **Hyatt Ziva / Hyatt Zilara**\n- **Secrets, Dreams or Breathless**\n- **Hilton Hotels & Resorts or Curio Collection**\n- **Westin, Sheraton or Autograph Collection All-Inclusive**\n- **Iberostar Selection**\n- **Paradisus by Meliá**\n- **Barceló, RIU Palace or similar established resort operators**\n- **Grand Fiesta Americana or Live Aqua**\n\n### Practical “core six” for an initial RFP\n\nFor a typical urban or mixed-use upper-upscale project, a balanced initial slate might be:\n\n1. **Westin or Renaissance**\n2. **Autograph Collection**\n3. **Hilton or Curio Collection**\n4. **Hyatt Regency or Hyatt Centric**\n5. **Hotel Indigo or voco**\n6. **Grand Fiesta Americana or Curamoria**\n\nThe final shortlist should be adjusted for **destination, room count, meeting-space intensity, new-build versus conversion, franchise versus management structure, branded residences, all-inclusive format, and territorial availability**. Brand classification also varies slightly by industry source and individual property—particularly for collection brands that can span upper-upscale and luxury."
          }
